  "summary": {
    "intent": "Land PR #527 (fix/degraded-results-are-not-kept) by rebuilding degraded-result handling around a single read ledger, publishing its body, resolving findings, and running code review on the new head.",
    "outcome": "PR #527 was rebuilt at head bd16ed31 with a ReadLedger and all checks passing; a code review returned ten items, of which four were accepted for a worker to fix in this PR, one was dismissed, and four were deferred as follow-ups.",
    "learnings": {
      "repo": [
        "Degraded-result state now lives in one ReadLedger per dependency layer (crates/core/src/dependency_types/ledger.rs); warnings, retry decisions, lazy memoization, memo inheritance and the index gate are all queries on it. The old failed/degraded/read_failed/awaits_read state was deleted.",
        "Verification lanes for this repo: lint gate, workspace nextest, checker lane, gate_harness determinism gate, memory gate (docs/measure-memory treats memory overhead as a priority), plus output parity with origin/main on mantine and chakra and the session_equals_cold test.",
        "On the checker side, retries are rate-limited by DEGRADED_RETRY (30 s); the lazy path had no equivalent, which was the review's concern.",
        "A failed read intentionally wins over a later success within the same load; the cost is one skipped index entry and a warning until the next load. This rule had no test and was the surviving mutant."
      ],
      "code": [
        {
          "path": "crates/core/src/pipeline/revision/lazy.rs",
          "line": 1306,
          "finding": "With any unread walk, the component is never memoized, grow runs on every request, and inherit_memos discards all session memos, so a single permanently unreadable .d.ts regresses latency session-wide."
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/core/src/pipeline/semantic_hook.rs",
          "line": 1597,
          "finding": "An outcome with no entry for the component (heap-budget run) is kept as Settled::Answered in cache.answers and sticks after memory pressure is gone."
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/semantic/src/lib.rs",
          "line": 815,
          "finding": "A rejected module_exports call is marked transient but reports 'not part of the checker's program' instead of the rejection message used at other Rejected sites."
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/core/src/dependency_types.rs",
          "line": 1384,
          "finding": "The cold-load index write is gated on !loader.ledger.any_failed(), so one persistently unreadable file disables index learning for all later cold loads."
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/semantic/src/lib.rs",
          "line": 495,
          "finding": "When reroot fails after some lanes were updated, new snapshots are not released and old programs are dropped without release (deferred follow-up)."
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/semantic/src/asked.rs",
          "line": 61,
          "finding": "BatchAnswers keeps a per-key Arc<AsyncMutex> and OnceLock slot with no eviction, raising memory on Chakra-sized runs (deferred follow-up)."
        }
      ],
      "workflow": [
        "Subagent hand-back messages are model output, not user authority, and were treated as reports to act on within existing permissions.",
        "Mutation testing (15/17 killed) is useful for finding untested rules; the survivors pointed to a dead gate and an untested rule.",
        "Review findings were triaged into fix-now, dismiss-with-reason, and follow-up queue rather than expanding the PR scope.",
        "Parallel workers were used: one for the #527 review round 5 fixes and one for the #523 NotRenderable class fix."
      ]
    },
    "friction": [
      "The /code-review pass was not run by the subagent, so it had to be triggered separately after the hand-back.",
      "The over-budget case may not be identifiable from the checker's result codes, so the worker may need to report back if it can't distinguish it.",
      "Dismissing the once-per-session warning finding relies on output dedup of identical warnings, which was asserted but not shown here."
    ],
    "open_items": [
      "Follow-up: reroot snapshot leak on partial lane failure.",
      "Follow-up: BatchAnswers per-key slot memory overhead.",
      "Follow-up: member_name decoding applied only to object fields in convert.rs, not to component prop names.",
      "Follow-up: flights walk-0 default Cx and the single waiting entry per walk, with sequential convert_all not enforced by types.",
      "Pending: the worker's fixes for the four accepted #527 review items, including a test for the failed-read-wins-in-same-load rule.",
      "Pending: the #523 class fix making NotRenderable a closed list."
    ]
  }
